From: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media/gpu: enable AV1 hardware decode for V4L2 on Linux

use_av1_hw_decoder is gated on VA-API when building for Linux:

    use_av1_hw_decoder =
        is_chromeos || (is_linux && use_vaapi) || is_win || is_apple

so a desktop Linux build configured with use_v4l2_codec=true and
use_vaapi=false gets no AV1 hardware decoder at all, even on hardware
whose V4L2 decoder advertises AV1. Nothing reports this: the AV1 support
is simply absent from the build, the browser falls back to the software
decoder, and about:gpu lists no AV1 entry, so it reads as "this hardware
cannot do AV1" rather than "this build has it compiled out".

The V4L2 side is otherwise ready. media/gpu/v4l2/v4l2_utils.cc already
defines the stateful AV1 pixel format

    #define V4L2_PIX_FMT_AV1 v4l2_fourcc('A', 'V', '0', '1')

and v4l2_device.cc already accepts V4L2_PIX_FMT_AV1 and
V4L2_PIX_FMT_AV1_FRAME when enumerating supported formats. Only the
buildflag keeps the decoder out.

Add use_v4l2_codec to the Linux condition, which matches what is_chromeos
already implies for V4L2-based devices.

Tested on a CIX Sky1 (Radxa Orion O6, Arm Linlon MVE v8 VPU) whose decoder
reports:

    v4l2-ctl -d /dev/video0 --list-formats-out
    ...
    [7]: 'AV01' (AV1 OBU Stream, compressed, dyn-resolution)

That the VPU decodes AV1 correctly through V4L2 was verified independently
of Chromium: an ffmpeg build with a V4L2 AV1 m2m decoder produced output
bit-identical to the dav1d software decoder (matching MD5 over the first
five frames of a 720p AV1 clip).

Bug: none
Change-Id: I0000000000000000000000000000000000000000

diff --git a/media/gpu/args.gni b/media/gpu/args.gni
--- a/media/gpu/args.gni
+++ b/media/gpu/args.gni
@@ -57,7 +57,7 @@ use_linux_video_acceleration = use_vaapi || use_v4l2_codec
 declare_args() {
   # A platform that is capable of hardware av1 decoding.
   use_av1_hw_decoder =
-      is_chromeos || (is_linux && use_vaapi) || is_win || is_apple
+      is_chromeos || (is_linux && (use_vaapi || use_v4l2_codec)) ||
+      is_win || is_apple
 }
